--- linux-7.2.8/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/README.md	1970-01-01 01:00:00.000000000 +0100
+++ linux-7.2.8/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/README.md	2026-10-02 08:55:53.000000000 +0200
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# meson-amvdec — stateless V4L2 driver for the openucode firmware
+
+gus bourg's stateless rework of Maxime Jourdan's meson vdec driver (public
+`gusbourg/linux` branch `amlogic-vdec/rfc`, 0b9101e, with Christian Hewitt's
+patches), carrying the openucode firmware paths. It loads **only** the four
+openucode images (`meson/vdec/ompeg2_sl.bin`, `oh264_sl.bin`, `ohevc_sl.bin`,
+`ovp9_sl.bin`); both firmware loaders refuse any other name. Stateless
+(request API) only. Private: this tree lives in openucode only.
+
+`CHANGES.md` lists the base, the patches applied, what was ported from the
+previous openucode driver, what was removed (all vendor-firmware code), and
+every adaptation.
+
+| SoC | MPEG-2 | H.264 | HEVC | VP9 |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| GXBB, GXL, GXLX, GXM | 1080p | 1080p | 8-bit 1080p (verified on GXBB) | — |
+| G12A, G12B, SM1 | 1080p | 4K | Main/Main 10 up to 4096x2304, NV12M + AM21C | profile 0/2 4K, NV12M + AM21C |
+
+Build (out of tree):
+
+    make -C <kernel build dir> M=$PWD ARCH=arm64 CROSS_COMPILE=<prefix> modules
+    #   BUNDLE_H264=1   kernels without CONFIG_V4L2_H264 (carries v4l2-h264.c)
+    #   OUCODE_DEV=1    development build: amrisc-test debugfs harness,
+    #                   *_bench / *_prof / debug parameters
+
+`insmod meson-amvdec.ko` needs no parameters (unload the staging
+`meson_vdec` first). `tools/`: record-builder equivalence tests against the
+Python host models (`ohevc_rec_gen.py` + `ohevc_rec_test.c`, `ovp9_rec_*`).
+`tests/`: AMRISC test images for the harness. `OPEN_H264.md`: H.264 path
+design and record mapping.
